WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 43 - The Forgotten Wilderness

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.120
All right, okay!

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.240
So, this is where <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> will be staged.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.670
That's right. But as a stage, it's not yet complete.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.570
When the acting changes, the props have to change too.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:59.340
Just remember that it's not done yet.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.680
Baron.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.570
I want you to play your part off Stewart, the young anthropologist.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:05.800
Yes, sir!

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.810
"Stewart!"

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:13.470
"There's still a lot left for you to learn in this field!"

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.040
Now, be more timid!

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:22.770
"You're still... you only know what humans are like from books."

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.790
Now, more lethargic!

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.550
"Are you even listening?"

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:28.520
"You hear me? Never forget:

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:34.320
We're animals too."

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:39.560
"You only know what humans are like from books..."

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.730
Now, retaliate, Stewart!

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.630
"But we're cultured animals!"

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.910
"The size of our brains and our bone structures are completely different!"

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.900
And now, I want to see an angry baron and a lethargic Stewart.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.430
"You hear me? Never forget:

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:59.500
We're animals too."

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:03.610
"But we're cultured animals..."

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.870
How interesting. Just by changing the mood of the roles,

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.840
the feel of the play transforms completely.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.310
I'm going to create a living play with this piece.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.890
A living play?

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.510
Don't worry. We'll do things normally for the first few nights.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.970
We're not going to change any of the lines or the cues,

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:29.400
but don't forget that countless plays can spring forth from just one script.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.340
So, I guess even Ryuuzo Kuronuma is getting serious now.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:38.250
Yes. He conducts his rehearsals differently than he used to.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.630
I'm sorry, but Mr. Masumi currently has a visitor.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.600
I'll wait here if that's all right.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.610
My, he has so many books!

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.090
He won't let himself switch off, even when he's by himself.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.410
<i>Psychology, Space, Space, Space, Business Psychology, Law, Summer Constellations</i>

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.500
What's this?

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:08.500
What does this girl mean to you, Mr. Masumi?

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.500
<i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.190
At last! Our opening night is tomorrow.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:15.080
Now, some of you have never performed in front of an audience before,

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:17.520
but if we can make it through today's dress rehearsal, you'll all do just fine.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:24.300
Everybody make sure to double-check there's nothing wrong with your costumes or your props.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:29.540
Sakurakouji! I brought you a little something!

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.120
I made it myself!

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.800
Thank you, Mai.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:43.190
There's a delivery for you, Maya.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:50.110
These are to wish you success on your opening night.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:54.460
When will he come to see the show?

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.980
He will be here tomorrow for your opening performance.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.560
Really?!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:03.270
He's a very busy person, but he honors his promises.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:08.650
Just knowing that he'll be in the theater tomorrow makes me very happy.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:14.290
Please tell him that I'll give it my all!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.770
I shall do just that.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.480
A strong typhoon, dubbed Typhoon #9, is heading northeast from the sea, south of Honshu.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.310
It will hit the Kanto region at around eight o'clock tonight...

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.250
Does this mean we'll have to cancel our show, Mr. Kuronuma?

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.630
Under no circumstances shall we cancel our show!

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.010
We've already sold tickets.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:37.830
As long as we have at least one person in the audience, the curtain will go up.

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:41.770
This has turned out to be a pretty harsh opening night, hasn't it, Maya?

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.210
You said it.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.410
We used to talk about this when we were younger...

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.690
You know, about how great it would be to perform on the same stage together.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:54.700
Now I've finally managed to get up on stage with you!

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.260
So, you're going out, no matter what I say?

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:10.770
Miss, you can't possibly go out on a day like this!

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:15.730
Even on a day like this, there are people who have the courage to put on a play.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:18.640
I'm going. Please prepare the car!

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:33.260
Miss, the roads appear to be closed.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.790
But, that's impossible!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.740
This road has been closed too!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.810
Mr. Masumi!

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.800
I'll walk.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.720
According to the National Weather Service, Typhoon Nine is moving up the coast...

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:56.020
with a velocity of 20km/h. The Kanto region is...

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.740
The road in front of the theater has been closed too!

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:02.770
Sir, it's show time and we haven't even got a single person in the audience...

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.100
The judges from the Acting Festival and the representatives from the board...

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.720
were meant to come tonight.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:15.720
But I wanted you to see it most of all, Mr. Purple Roses.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:24.220
The start time has come and gone. I'm very sorry, everyone, but today's show is...

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:33.640
Mr. Hayami!

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:37.710
What's the matter? Shouldn't this show have started by now?

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:41.270
Or did I get the starting time wrong?

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.140
Please begin.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:55.130
Why have you come on a day like this, Mr. Hayami?

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:59.350
Weren't you the one who invited me?

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.290
I told you I'd keep my promise.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.720
You came all the way over here in a typhoon just to keep a promise?

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.320
Why would you do something like that?

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:09.470
Start already.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.160
I came here to watch you on stage.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:19.390
Yes, please watch then! I'm going to show you a Jane that I'm not ashamed to show you!

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:22.390
If the acting's poor, I have no qualms about leaving halfway through.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.550
I wouldn't put it past you!

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:27.090
Places, everyone!

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.280
Let's go, Maya.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:36.280
Right, everyone! It's show time!

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:43.880
There's only one person in the audience and it's Mr. Hayami.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.640
Please, I want you to stay in your seat until the very end.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:53.930
Mr. Hayami, watch my Jane!

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.680
The year is 1928.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:07.920
Two naked girls were discovered in the Carpathian Mountains,

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.380
living with a pack of wolves and walking around on all fours.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.000
The rumors were true! Grab her!

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:17.960
Get her!

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:19.930
She's gonna bite!

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.940
She's over there! Rope her in!

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:29.810
When I watch you, I don't see it as a mere performance.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:35.640
Where do you hide this overwhelming passion in that small body of yours?

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:41.090
Good. Draw me in even more.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:51.080
<i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:55.400
Her breakfast is raw meat and water in equal measures.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.160
One cup of milk.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.680
She gets sleepy during the day.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.980
The wolf's daily routine doesn't seem to lessen in her.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:11.330
Music seems to irritate her.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:15.130
Mirrors interest her.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.560
It's a blackout!

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.120
Everyone, stay calm!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.810
We're going to look for some flashlights!

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:46.230
Maya. You've kept on acting this whole time.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:51.220
When you're on stage, you're Jane until the final curtain.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.760
She doesn't drop her mask, even when it's pitch black.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.270
Jane, come here!

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.810
It's teatime, everyone!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.540
Thank you.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.140
Jane only eats from my hand, though.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:10.630
So, the play has started to gather pace.

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:12.790
I told you not to walk around on all fours anymore!

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:23.520
That's right. That scarf smells like me.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.270
Stewa-

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.210
That's right! That's me!

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:30.470
Stewa-

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:34.130
Jane, that's you!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.110
Jane!

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:45.390
Jane! That's right! You're one of us! You're human!

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.850
Really?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.950
All right.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.890
Thank you.

00:11:55.380 --> 00:12:01.010
You went out in a typhoon like this just to see her show, Mr. Masumi?

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:05.020
Do you remember this blue scarf?

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:10.220
This is the scarf that made you first say my name.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.670
Think about me sometime...

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.930
Goodbye, Jane.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:21.280
I am a girl.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:23.960
I am fifteen years old.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:27.340
I am human.

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:31.540
Stewart!

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.070
What's wrong, everyone?

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:51.890
I'm waiting for the curtain call!

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:54.000
Thank you very much!

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:59.630
That was a good play!

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.180
Please keep up the good work until the final day.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:06.860
The lights are back on!

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.600
Hold it right there, young Hayami!

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.960
You managed to get here, even on a day like this.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:16.040
It's because of you that everyone was able to give their all.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.610
Please, celebrate our opening night with us.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:22.590
Until this typhoon blows over, let's party!

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:28.030
Thank you very much for coming on such a day,

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:32.270
and for staying in your seat until the end.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:37.860
It's not like you to thank me, little one.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:44.640
Your Jane was wonderful. She was definitely the best.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:50.520
If you really mean that, then I'm happy.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:56.720
His hair's soaking wet.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:07.610
Little one...

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:17.720
If you don't dry off, you'll catch a cold.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.170
Thank you, but that's enough.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.780
This is Stewart's blue scarf.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:34.020
The scene where Jane slowly realizes her humanity while sniffing this scarf was very moving.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:37.680
Thank you for coming tonight, Mr. Hayami.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.270
Sakurakouji!

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.630
You're going to become a nuisance for Mr. Hayami if you keep nattering away like that.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:45.310
Mr. Kuronuma wants you to get changed.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.310
A storm...

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:57.030
And it doesn't look like the storm inside me is going to end anytime soon either.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:05.270
Mr. Hayami left in the middle of this typhoon?!

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.600
Mr. Hayami!

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:16.690
I feel strange...

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:20.290
Aren't I meant to hate him?

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.830
What?

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:28.400
You're telling me that Mr. Hayami braved that typhoon to see <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>?

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:32.810
Yes, Daito Corporation is continuing to prepare for <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>,

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:37.800
and Ryuuzo Kuronuma has apparently been named as a contender for the role of director.

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:38.400
What?

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.030
For <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>?

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:46.670
Yes. And Yuu Sakurakouji is being considered as the male lead.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.380
Which means that, including her,

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:52.040
<i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> has three candidates for <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:59.970
Mr. Masumi, was it because of <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> that you braved the storm that night?

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.500
Or was it because...

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:09.010
This can't be happening! Why would all of these famous actors come here of all places?

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:11.620
And those are the judges from the Acting Festival!

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:17.600
I don't understand this turnout when this play isn't even eligible for the Acting Festival.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:23.370
Stay focused, people. Do exactly what you did in front of Mr. Hayami last night.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:27.520
I know the opening night was disrupted by a typhoon,

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:32.440
but I'm sure you'll come see one of our performances, Mr. Purple Roses.

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:48.610
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:59.740
Her older sister died because her body grew weak.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:08.310
She was the wolf girl's only friend. Now, she's lost her one and only companion in this world.

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:13.250
Her sorrow is bottomless and every day, she returns to the same spot where her sister used to be...

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:16.510
and sniffs around, refusing to leave that spot without being coaxed.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:22.600
Afterwards, her appetite failed and she stopped eating altogether.

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:31.860
That's the expressionless anguish of a wild animal.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.600
I didn't know such an expression existed!

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:50.710
From now on, this is your home, Jane.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:55.520
From tomorrow morning onwards, you won't live in a cage. You're going to become human, Jane!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:06.380
He's got pneumonia, brought on by wandering around outside all night.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:08.110
Forgive us, Stewart!

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:12.350
Oh Lord, please save this young man.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:16.350
What will happen to that girl if she loses the only man she can rely on?

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:17.820
Stewart!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.360
Stewa-!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:28.280
That's not the same vacant expression she wore before...

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:29.160
This is...

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:31.860
Hang in there, Stewart! You can't die!

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.310
How are you able to take it so far?

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:44.410
When you become the real thing, the people around you change with you.

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:48.210
The stage is overflowing with life.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.270
You're a true actress.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:55.320
I've never once considered myself to have won against you.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.150
Stewart!

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:04.340
Stewart!

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.600
Jane, you've got it!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:10.530
The scent on that red scarf is my scent!

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:13.580
Stewart. That's me!

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:16.540
I am Jane.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:19.440
I am human.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:23.050
Come quickly, everyone! Jane's got it!

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:50.040
That was great. Truly moving.

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:53.770
I didn't expect to hear praise from you, Mr. Fujimi, the organizer of the Acting Festival...

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:59.290
The difference in acting between the wild instincts and the human emotion was spectacular.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:04.620
We will reconsider admitting this play for the Acting Festival right away.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:11.010
Sir, would it be possible to ask you to come and see this show again in five days' time?

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:16.170
I do not intend to keep this play as it was today.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:20.020
I'd like to challenge this play's potential.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:25.000
Smash Hit! Wolf Girl!
<i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> is now a contender for top gongs in the Acting Festival.

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.140
They say we're going to be in the Acting Festival!

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:30.900
They want to interview me?

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:33.650
It's an older man. He's in the lobby.

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:38.150
Do you remember me, miss?

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:42.870
You handed me a flyer for this play at the train station.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.970
Oh yeah, we had a coffee together!

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:49.780
You actually came!

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.150
How did you like the show?

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:54.140
It was wonderful!

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:55.950
Really?

00:20:55.950 --> 00:21:01.000
Now, no one else can play this role after you.

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:05.400
You've acted out the perfect Jane.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:11.630
Let's meet again, Miss Maya.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:23.470
You've all done great.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.880
Good job!

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:30.340
However, like I said, this is just the beginning.

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:34.410
Now, we'll create an entirely new play!

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:37.120
A different <i>Forgotten Wilderness</i>!

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:41.480
A different <i>Forgotten Wilderness</i>?

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:45.900
That's right! The lines won't change, but the acting will!

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.800
So, let's start rehearsing!

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.100
Let's go!

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello hello

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello, hello.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Fukanou dato iwarenagara tobitatte

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Even though they say it's impossible, I fly off.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
Kanaeta yume mo koboreochita yume mo aru

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
There are dreams that come true, and dreams that crumble away.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
Soredemo isshoukenmei ikiru kazu dake hoshi ga fueru

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
But even then, for every person trying hard to live their life, a new star is born.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Kyou mo mata hitotsu umareru hoshi miagete

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Today, I look up again, at another newly born star.

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello hello another star

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello, hello another star.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change.

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
Ai wo daite norikonda shatoru

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
I've boarded the shuttle with my love.

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Daremo ga hitori no uchuuhikoushi dayo

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Every single person is an astronaut.

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
Negau yume kara yume e

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
From fulfilled dream to dream,

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
Dokomademo yukeru one life

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
I can go anywhere... One life.

00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:25.450
The cues and the lines may be the same,

00:23:25.450 --> 00:23:30.390
but depending on the mood of the acting, a living play can become a comedy or a tragedy.

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:34.430
A single play unfolds into limitless possibilities.

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.290
I've never had to work so hard before.

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:41.450
And on top of that, Ms. Tsukikage has...

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:44.220
Ms. Tsukikage, please open your eyes!

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:47.350
We haven't even got to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> yet!

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:51.580
Episode 44 - An Infinite Play
